<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Ampolex announces revised note plan.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Ampolex announces revised note plan.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil and gas producer Ampolex Ltd said on Wednesday that holders of its convertible notes were to consider a revised proposal under which Mobil Corp will buy the notes at A$10 each.</p>
<p>The proposal would be considered on November 28. Mobil holds 97 percent of the convertible notes after reaching a settlement in September with Sir Ron Brierley's Guiness Peat Group (GPG) Plc about the correct conversion rate.</p>
<p>Mobil also owns more than 99 percent of Ampolex ordinary and preference shares following its A$1.36 billion bid.  </p>
<p>The convertible notes, suspended from trading on Tuesday, would be reinstated to trading on Wednesday, Ampolex said</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
